        <p>I've worked with more than 150 students on the SAT and ACT. Many of them came to me anxious and overwhelmed by math and test-taking. I didn't start with this approach as a theory. Working with those students is what led me to build it.</p>
        <p>I hold a BA in Physics and a BS in Mathematics from SUNY New Paltz, where I later taught math to undergraduate business students. I spent years at an elite test-prep firm in New York, earned an MBA from UCLA Anderson, and became a certified HeartMath&reg; trainer.</p>
        <p>I had great mentors as a student, and I owe a lot of my path to them. That's the role I take with every student: a guide in their corner who knows the territory.</p>
        <p>Test day matters, but it was never the whole point. The skills that steady a student on test day are the ones they'll carry into every high-stakes moment after it.</p>
